From 47d4415d432c1439fbf602f55e8dffa91ebb5dcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:47:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] feat(kubevirt): vm_lifecycle run_policy; restart keeps
 the VM's run strategy (K8S-13)

vm_lifecycle start sets runStrategy Always (documented), and restart
stops the VM and sets Always too, so a restart silently turned Manual,
RerunOnFailure or Once into Always (K8S-13; the refuter narrowed the
undocumented part to restart). Restart was also two plain updates of a
possibly stale object, which upstream found conflicting with
virt-controller on live clusters.

Following upstream PR #1655 (open, a recreation of #1012):
- a `run_policy` argument with #1655's values: HighAvailability
  (runStrategy Always), RestartOnFailure (RerunOnFailure), Once. start
  defaults to HighAvailability, as before and as in #1655;
- every run-strategy update re-reads the VM and retries on a conflict.

In addition to #1655: restart without run_policy keeps the VM's own run
strategy (Always if it was Halted or unset), and its answer names the
strategy it set. That is the part a comment on #1655 would raise;
#1655 itself keeps Always as the restart default.

The existing start, stop and restart tests (Halted VMs) are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
